#: ../../source/docs/ac_tipsfornewpilots.rst:5
#: 21ad78cdb6934cecac90a88d11156123
msgid "Tips For New Pilots"
msgstr "新手飞行技巧"

#: ../../source/docs/ac_tipsfornewpilots.rst:7
#: 0f63529f709a42668d2c74edd2c9e2ff
msgid ""
"This page gives some advice on initial flying strategies for those with "
"limited or no previous experience flying RC aircraft or multicopters."
msgstr "本页面为无或仅有少量 RC 飞机或多旋翼飞行经验的用户提供初次飞行策略建议。"

#: ../../source/docs/ac_tipsfornewpilots.rst:11
#: 3205bd937f644e39a1c893240a998396
msgid "First flight"
msgstr "首次飞行"

#: ../../source/docs/ac_tipsfornewpilots.rst:13
#: cf43ee598a6c4ce6a464d51c8694010e
msgid ""
"Place the copter on level ground and connect the battery — do not move the "
"copter until gyroscope calibration is completed (LED's flashing red and "
"blue). Ensure that your RC mode toggle switch is in Stabilize mode. Slowly "
"raise the throttle until the copter just lifts off the ground."
msgstr ""
"将飞机放置在水平地面上并连接电池——在陀螺仪校准完成之前（LED 红蓝交替闪烁）请勿移动飞机。确认 RC 模式切换开关处于 Stabilize "
"模式。缓慢推高油门直到飞机刚好离地。"

#: ../../source/docs/ac_tipsfornewpilots.rst:18
#: edc98793fb6143a2b1dcdaa5de090301
msgid ""
"If it seems like it's going to flip or otherwise isn't lifting straight up "
"it is possible that you've set the wrong +/x orientation, hooked up your "
"motors in the wrong order or have the prop direction or pusher/puller order "
"wrong. You can test this by following the instructions in :ref:`connect-"
"escs-and-motors_testing_motor_spin_directions`."
msgstr ""
"若飞机看起来要翻转或无法垂直起飞，可能是方向设置错误（+/X）、电机接线顺序错误或螺旋桨方向/推拉顺序错误。可按 :ref:`connect-escs-"
"and-motors_testing_motor_spin_directions` 中的说明进行测试。"

#: ../../source/docs/ac_tipsfornewpilots.rst:24
#: d82e52b651f14d3d8993ca2725e72da1
msgid ""
"If any of the controls are reversed (pitch or roll are backwards, meaning "
"the copter moves in the opposite direction as your stick), you'll need to "
"reverse the affected channel at your RC transmitter side. Please see your RC"
" transmitter's manual if you're not familiar with the process. It's a good "
"idea to re-do your RC calibration in the Mission Planner after you've "
"reversed a channel."
msgstr ""
"若控制方向反了（俯仰或横滚反向，即飞机朝摇杆反方向运动），需在 RC 遥控器端反转相应通道。如不熟悉操作请参阅遥控器说明书。反转通道后最好在 "
"Mission Planner 中重新进行 RC 校准。"

#: ../../source/docs/ac_tipsfornewpilots.rst:31
#: ae56b2b5a0a34afa844aa45010145755
msgid ""
"If it lifts off smoothly, you may see a little yaw. That shouldn't be more "
"than about 30 degrees and will correct itself with more flying time. There "
"should be no pronounced wobble (if there is, you may have an unbalanced prop"
" or out-of-true motor)."
msgstr "若起飞平稳，可能会有轻微偏航，不超过约 30 度，并会随飞行时间自行修正。不应有明显抖动（若有，可能是螺旋桨不平衡或电机不正）。"

#: ../../source/docs/ac_tipsfornewpilots.rst:36
#: d919589561f544b58777cd0d509d595f
msgid ""
"The copter should also tend to stay in place, and you shouldn't have to "
"fight strong tendencies to move left or right or forward or back. If you do "
"see that behavior, do NOT use your RC trims to correct (this just throws off"
" the calibration). Instead, it probably means that the copter may not have "
"been completely flat during calibration or the airframe is out of true (one "
"motor tilted). Land and correct that."
msgstr ""
"飞机应保持基本位置不变，无需对抗强烈的左右或前后飘移趋势。若出现此现象，请勿使用 RC "
"微调来修正（这只会影响校准）。这可能意味着校准时飞机未完全水平，或机架未对齐（某个电机倾斜）。降落后进行修正。"

#: ../../source/docs/ac_tipsfornewpilots.rst:43
#: 5595cc8565bd4e40b59fbe6bbe2667b2
msgid ""
"If you're having trouble and the copter is not hovering smoothly, run "
"through the :ref:`troubleshooting guide <troubleshooting>`."
msgstr "如遇到困难且飞机无法平稳悬停，请参考 :ref:`故障排查指南 <troubleshooting>`。"

#: ../../source/docs/ac_tipsfornewpilots.rst:46
#: cb7a880b758c48a89f4820e7c7f4c193
msgid ""
"Assuming that all is fine so far, you're ready for more advanced modes, such"
" as Alt Hold and Loiter."
msgstr "假设到目前为止一切正常，您已准备好尝试更高级的模式，如 Alt Hold 和 Loiter。"

#: ../../source/docs/ac_tipsfornewpilots.rst:50
#: 675477e8f98a4161ba8a60e57ccb2092
msgid "Tips for your first flights"
msgstr "首次飞行技巧"

#: ../../source/docs/ac_tipsfornewpilots.rst:52
#: 596adbdaa67a47abb3d889b60d771c30
msgid ""
"Make sure you are in a wind free environment (wind will play against you on "
"in air auto trim)."
msgstr "确保在无风环境中飞行（风会干扰空中自动配平）。"

#: ../../source/docs/ac_tipsfornewpilots.rst:54
#: 9787e3f10c3f48239bb1ab8199aaeb43
msgid ""
"Make sure you have no trim on your Radio (the autopilot is what we want to "
"trim, the radio should never get trimmed)."
msgstr "确保遥控器上没有微调（我们希望调整飞控，遥控器不应微调）。"

#: ../../source/docs/ac_tipsfornewpilots.rst:56
#: 435fd74286004661921c661c7de217c4
msgid ""
"Hold the copter still and level after connecting the battery to allow the "
"gyroscopes to initialize."
msgstr "连接电池后保持飞机静止水平，等待陀螺仪初始化。"

#: ../../source/docs/ac_tipsfornewpilots.rst:58
#: 8d90471f70a84d6db736e41184638d0f
msgid "Get above ground effect, around 3-4 feet is enough on most models."
msgstr "离地面效应区，在大多数机型上约 3-4 英尺即可。"

#: ../../source/docs/ac_tipsfornewpilots.rst:59
#: 69e2598390994d7a84d6efc414ec7aa2
msgid ""
"Make sure to practice a lot before you actually try the auto trim to find "
"the sweet spot on the Radio right stick to have the copter super stable and "
"not moving (This is where wind affect your inputs)."
msgstr "在真正尝试自动配平之前要大量练习，找到遥控器右摇杆的甜蜜点，使飞机超级稳定且不漂移（这正是风对输入产生影响的地方）。"

#: ../../source/docs/ac_tipsfornewpilots.rst:63
#: fbe18544089340599feb8ac31ce6266d
msgid ""
"We recommend not starting in Simple mode. Begin your flying in the basic "
"Stabilize mode."
msgstr "建议不要从 Simple 模式开始。从基础的 Stabilize 模式开始飞行。"

#: ../../source/docs/ac_tipsfornewpilots.rst:65
#: 15b0999281004bfb8b703a09e92fdd5d
msgid ""
"Copter establishes its home position at the time of arming, so arm your "
"copter in the location you wish to designate as the home position."
msgstr "Copter 在解锁时建立其返航位置，请在您希望设为返航点的位置解锁飞机。"

#: ../../source/docs/ac_tipsfornewpilots.rst:70
#: 34a6ee89ebcd4063a69a7cf710f7b564
msgid "Warning about low batteries"
msgstr "低电量警告"

#: ../../source/docs/ac_tipsfornewpilots.rst:72
#: 1f920a27808f412cac940ba808fbc442
msgid ""
"When flying a VTOL vehicle, you need to keep in mind that it flies much "
"differently than a winged airplane. In an airplane, lift is generated by the"
" wing and you still have control surfaces for maneuvering if the motor were "
"to stop. QuadPlanes and Multicopters generate lift solely from the thrust of"
" the motors, so if your battery is excessively depleted, you have no lift "
"and no control over your vehicle, and it may flip over and crash without a "
"gradual warning. During first flights, fly only short durations until you "
"know your battery consumption and use one of the following batteries "
"monitoring methods to ensure that you always have enough power remaining to "
"safely land your copter (and not ruin the battery)."
msgstr ""
"驾驶 VTOL 飞行器时，需记住它的飞行方式与有翼飞机大不相同。飞机的升力由机翼产生，即使电机停转仍有控制面可供机动。QuadPlane "
"和多旋翼的升力完全来自电机推力，因此若电池过度亏电，将失去升力和对飞行器的控制，可能在没有渐进征兆的情况下翻转坠毁。首次飞行时，请只飞短时间，直到你了解电池消耗情况，并使用以下电池监控方法之一，确保始终有足够剩余电量安全降落飞行器（且不损坏电池）。"

#: ../../source/docs/ac_tipsfornewpilots.rst:83
#: faba23a905004e959f1bd8681bd18a64
msgid ""
"ArduPilot supports Battery voltage monitoring. For more information, visit "
"the :ref:`3DR Power Module for Measuring Voltage and Current <common-3dr-"
"power-module>` page."
msgstr ""
"ArduPilot 支持电池电压监控。更多信息请访问 :ref:`用于测量电压和电流的 3DR 电源模块 <common-3dr-power-"
"module>` 页面。"

#: ../../source/docs/ac_tipsfornewpilots.rst:84
#: c4114c50cf7e423c87fa906d72891532
msgid ""
"You may also program your ESCs to use a slow or no cutoff at low voltages."
msgstr "您也可以将电调编程为低电压时慢速或不断电。"

#: ../../source/docs/ac_tipsfornewpilots.rst:86
#: 935420eb6eea4cff97cf7b6263fbda16
msgid ""
"For autopilots without power module it is HIGHLY recommended you install a "
":ref:`Battery Voltage Monitor <common-powermodule-landingpage>`."
msgstr "对于没有电源模块的飞控，强烈建议安装 :ref:`电池电压监控器 <common-powermodule-landingpage>`。"

#: ../../source/docs/ac_tipsfornewpilots.rst:89
#: 23b242760a7c413b8e81df21f54781ec
msgid ""
"For 3S LiPo batteries, the two wires can be soldered to the P-PCB directly, "
"or you can connect to the balancing plug of your battery."
msgstr "对于 3S LiPo 电池，两根导线可直接焊接到 P-PCB，或连接到电池的平衡插头。"

#: ../../source/docs/ac_tipsfornewpilots.rst:92
#: ab38054163cc41479ccf89eeb8533c23
msgid ""
"The battery voltage monitor linked above has a buzzer and LEDs that function"
" as follows:"
msgstr "上述电池电压监控器的蜂鸣器和 LED 功能如下："

#: ../../source/docs/ac_tipsfornewpilots.rst:129
#: 22f88a3a7cf34b0bacc478b932eb837c
msgid ""
"If you are using a battery monitor, always connect the main LiPo battery "
"wire before connecting the balancing port wire to the APM."
msgstr "如果使用电池监控器，请始终先连接主 LiPo 电池线，再将平衡口线连接到 APM。"

#: ../../source/docs/ac_tipsfornewpilots.rst:134
#: 5be1b4bd38f8495b9c3a7a3bd89cafb1
msgid "Motors RPM Check"
msgstr "电机 RPM 检查"

#: ../../source/docs/ac_tipsfornewpilots.rst:135
#: 87f6f6f628f44a22b6ded4ef49c3907b
msgid ""
"In modes where the vehicle takes off controlling the throttle itself (like "
"AUTO, LOITER, QLOITER, ALTHOLD, etc.), , and ESC telemetry is employed, the "
":ref:`TKOFF_RPM_MIN <TKOFF_RPM_MIN>` and :ref:`TKOFF_RPM_MAX "
"<TKOFF_RPM_MAX>` are monitored during the motor ramp up. See :ref:`common-"
"tkoff-rpm-min`."
msgstr ""
"在飞行器自行控制油门起飞的模式（如 AUTO、LOITER、QLOITER、ALTHOLD 等）下，若使用了电调数传，电机加速过程中会监控 "
":ref:`TKOFF_RPM_MIN <TKOFF_RPM_MIN>` 和 :ref:`TKOFF_RPM_MAX "
"<TKOFF_RPM_MAX>`。参见 :ref:`common-tkoff-rpm-min`。"
